<title>PAKISTAN: Pakistan slashes excise duty on telephone calls.</title>
<headline>Pakistan slashes excise duty on telephone calls.</headline>
<dateline>ISLAMABAD 1997-06-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Pakistan slashed excise duty on telephone calls to 25 percent from 40 percent in its budget for fiscal 1997/98 (July-June) on Friday.  </p>
<p>Finance Minister Sartaj Aziz said in his budget speech to the National Assembly (lower house) that the reduction was aimed at encouraging people to use telephones and to boost the mobile telephone sector, which has long complained of high taxation.</p>
<p>He said the government would urge the state-run Pakistan Telecommunication Company Ltd (PTCL) to reduce its tariffs for inter-city calls by 20 percent.</p>
<p>-- Islamabad newsroom 9251-274757</p>
</text>
